## Role

Members, onDuty, permission strings. TWO HONEST LIMITS, stated: `onDuty` is hand-set (no platform scheduler — rotation is a human act), and `permissions` is DATA read by workflow guards, not an ACL (realm permissions are the enforcement layer).

```ts
import { Role } from '@cardstack/catalog/cards/service-desk/role';

@field role = linksTo(() => Role);
```

### Non-goals

No duty rotation schedule; no identity — cards have no current-user concept, so actors are passed explicitly.
